menu "pcapx lab experiments"

    config LAB_PCAPX_EXP_DROP
        bool "DROP experiment: ring=2048, snaplen=64, N=500 UDP, no pacing"
        default n
        help
            Replaces the default capture session with a ring-overflow run:
            500 back-to-back UDP frames into a 2048-byte ring with snaplen=64
            must produce the contract log line "W pcapx: DROP cnt=N" and the
            packet accounting identity rx+tx == filtered+dropped+written
            (after the writer has drained the ring).

    config LAB_PCAPX_EXP_CHURN
        bool "CHURN experiment: attach/detach x100 under UDP traffic"
        default n
        help
            Runs a UDP traffic generator task and cycles pcapx attach/detach
            100 times while it is running. Success criteria: no crash, no
            heap leak (heap_caps_get_free_size before/after within noise).

endmenu
